{"type":"sense","headword":"serendipity","headwordNote":"独立名词，非其他词形变化","partOfSpeech":"noun","meaning":"意外发现美好事物的运气；机缘巧合；偶然的幸运发现","phonetic":"","register":"中性偏书面，常用于文学、评论和日常感叹","usageNote":"强调“并非刻意寻找，却意外得到好结果”，多带褒义和惊喜感；不可数，通常不用复数。","exampleEnglish":"Meeting my future wife in that tiny bookstore was pure serendipity.","exampleChinese":"在那家小书店遇见我未来的妻子，纯属机缘巧合。"}
{"type":"sense","headword":"serendipity","headwordNote":"独立名词，非其他词形变化","partOfSpeech":"noun","meaning":"（科学研究或探索中）意外发现珍奇事物的能力或现象","phonetic":"","register":"学术、科普语境","usageNote":"常用于描述科学史上因偶然机会获得重大发现的情形，如青霉素的发现。","exampleEnglish":"The discovery of penicillin is often cited as a classic example of serendipity in science.","exampleChinese":"青霉素的发现常被引为科学中机缘巧合的经典例子。"}
{"type":"usage","value":"serendipity 是不可数名词，指“意外收获好运”的过程或运气本身，常与 pure、sheer、a moment of 等搭配。它强调结果美好且非计划之中，与 luck（泛指的运气）和 coincidence（巧合，未必有好结果）不同。句型上多作主语或表语：It was pure serendipity that... / by serendipity。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"pure serendipity","meaning":"纯粹的机缘巧合","exampleEnglish":"Running into my old mentor at the airport was pure serendipity.","exampleChinese":"在机场偶遇我以前的导师，纯属机缘巧合。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"sheer serendipity","meaning":"十足的意外好运","exampleEnglish":"By sheer serendipity, the first hotel we tried had a free room.","exampleChinese":"纯属意外好运，我们试的第一家酒店正好有空房。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"a moment of serendipity","meaning":"机缘巧合的一刻","exampleEnglish":"Their collaboration began with a moment of serendipity at a conference.","exampleChinese":"他们的合作始于一次会议上的机缘巧合。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"by serendipity","meaning":"靠机缘巧合；偶然地","exampleEnglish":"She found the rare manuscript by serendipity while cleaning the attic.","exampleChinese":"她在清理阁楼时偶然发现了那份珍贵手稿。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"a stroke of serendipity","meaning":"一次意外的好运","exampleEnglish":"Getting that job was a stroke of serendipity.","exampleChinese":"得到那份工作是一次意外的好运。"}
{"type":"wordFamily","word":"serendipitous","partOfSpeech":"adjective","meaning":"意外发现美好事物的；机缘巧合的"}
{"type":"wordFamily","word":"serendipitously","partOfSpeech":"adverb","meaning":"机缘巧合地；偶然幸运地"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"chance","difference":"chance 指偶然性本身，中性，不保证结果美好；serendipity 强调偶然带来的是好结果。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"luck","difference":"luck 泛指好运或坏运，口语常用；serendipity 更书面，强调“意外发现”的过程。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"coincidence","difference":"coincidence 只指巧合，结果可好可坏；serendipity 带有积极、惊喜的色彩。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"fluke","difference":"fluke 多指侥幸的成功，常含“不太可能重复”的意味；serendipity 更优雅，强调发现之喜。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"fortuity","difference":"fortuity 非常正式且罕见，仅指偶然事件；serendipity 更常用且带褒义。"}
{"type":"memory","value":"源自波斯童话《锡兰三王子》（Serendip 是斯里兰卡旧称），王子们总在旅途中意外发现宝物，故 serendipity 即“意外发现珍宝的运气”。"}
{"type":"mistake","value":"serendipity 是不可数名词，不说 a serendipity 或 serendipities；要表示“一次”可用 a moment/stroke of serendipity。"}
{"type":"mistake","value":"不要把它简单等同于“运气好”：它强调在寻找别的东西时意外发现了好东西，若只是买彩票中奖，用 luck 更自然。"}
